          "mode": "exact",
          "quality": 0.07228915662650602,
          "answer": "VA life insurance offers financial security for Veterans, service members, and their families. There are several types of VA life insurance, including Servicemembers' Group Life Insurance (SGLI), Veterans' Group Life Insurance (VGLI), Service-Disabled Veterans Insurance (S-DVI), and Veterans Mortgage Life Insurance (VMLI) [S2].\n\nTo determine how much life insurance you need, the VA provides a **life insurance needs calculator** and a **VGLI comparison questionnaire** to help you decide [S1]. You can also find forms, handbooks, and guides on the VA website to help you apply for and manage your benefits [S1].\n\nIf you have a VA life insurance policy, you can **access and manage your policy online** through the VA or Prudential Insurance Company of America, depending on your policy type [S5]. This includes checking your policy status, paying premiums, and updating beneficiary information [S5].\n\nFor those with a **service-connected disability**, the **Service-Disabled Veterans Insurance (S-DVI)** program offers options. Premiums for the basic S-DVI policy may be waived for Veterans who are totally disabled [S6]. If you need assistance with your claim, you can contact the **VA Life Insurance Center at 800-669-8477** [S6].\n\nIf you're eligible for the **Specially Adapted Housing (SAH) Grant**, you may also qualify for **VMLI**, which helps your family pay off a home mortgage in the event of your death [S6].\n\nFor more information, visit the VA Life Insurance page or use the **SGLI Online Enrollment System (SOES)** if you're a service member [S1]. You can also contact the VA directly for help with claims, policy management, or appeals [S1]."
