          "prefill_tokens": 834,
          "mode": "infoflow",
          "quality": 0.035164835164835165,
          "answer": "The U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) offers several life insurance programs for Veterans, service members, and their families. These programs include Servicemembers' Group Life Insurance (SGLI), Veterans' Group Life Insurance (VGLI), Service-Disabled Veterans Insurance (S-DVI), and Veterans Mortgage Life Insurance (VMLI) [S2]. Here's a brief overview of these programs and how to access them:\n\n1. **Servicemembers' Group Life Insurance (SGLI):** This is a low-cost life insurance program available to active-duty service members. It provides up to $400,000 in coverage without a medical exam. You can enroll or make changes to your SGLI coverage through the SGLI Online Enrollment System (SOES) [S1].\n\n2. **Veterans' Group Life Insurance (VGLI):** VGLI allows Veterans who had SGLI coverage to convert their SGLI to a whole life insurance policy. The amount you can insure is based on your SGLI coverage at the time of separation from service. VGLI is available to Veterans for up to 12 months after leaving the military [S2].\n\n3. **Service-Disabled Veterans Insurance (S-DVI):** This program is for Veterans with a service-connected disability rated at least 10% by the VA. S-DVI offers low-cost life insurance to Veterans who may not qualify for other types of life insurance due to health issues [S6].\n\n4. **Veterans Mortgage Life Insurance (VMLI):** VMLI is a special type of life insurance that helps pay off the mortgage on a home that has been specially adapted for a Veteran with a severe service-connected disability. To qualify for VMLI, you must first apply for and receive a Specially Adapted Housing (SAH) Grant [S6].\n\nTo manage your VA life insurance policy, you can access your policy online, update your beneficiaries, file a claim, or pay your premium. You can also find out how much life insurance you need using the VA's life insurance needs calculator [S1]. If you have a VGLI policy, you can enroll in the VGLI Auto Pay feature to pay your premiums automatically from your bank account [S2].\n\nFor more information or to file a claim, you can contact the VA Life Insurance Center at 800-669-8477 [S6]. If you have a Veterans Group Life Insurance (VGLI) policy with a VGLI control number, you can access your policy through the Office of Servicemembers Group Life Insurance at Prudential Insurance Company of America [S5].\n\nIf you're considering converting your VA life insurance to a commercial policy, there are specific conditions and timeframes you should be aware of. It's also important to update your beneficiary information regularly to ensure that the proceeds from your policy go to the right people [S2].\n\nFor any questions about your VA life insurance policy or to find out if you're eligible for any of the VA's life insurance programs, you can use the VA's online resources or contact the VA directly. Remember to review the VA's publications and handbooks for detailed information on each of the life insurance programs [S1]."
